@page
@model GitHubModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "GitHub App";
    ViewData["Description"] = "A GitHub App that checks agent-authored pull requests for placeholders, stubs, tests without assertions, out-of-scope files and more.";
}

<section class="hero">
    <h1>Review agent pull requests.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The Aibysitter GitHub App reads every pull request in a repository where it is installed. It posts a check named Aibysitter review, with an annotation on each line it flags.</p>
    <p class="install-status"><strong>Install coming soon.</strong> The App is in testing.</p>
    <p><a asp-page="/Privacy">What the App reads and keeps</a></p>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <h2>What it flags</h2>
    <ul class="marks">
        @foreach (var row in Model.Checks)
        {
            <li><a asp-page="/Rules/Rule" asp-route-id="@row.Doc.Id">@row.Doc.Id</a> @row.Doc.Summary <span class="note">@row.Severity</span></li>
        }
    </ul>
</section>

<figure class="terminal" aria-label="Example check run">
    <pre><code><span class="t-prompt">check</span> Aibysitter review  <span class="t-prompt">conclusion</span> neutral
<span class="t-sum">4 findings (3 errors, 1 warning)</span>
<span class="t-loc">docs/notes.txt:1           </span> <span class="t-sev t-error">failure</span> <span class="t-rule">P004</span>  Outside declared scope (added): docs/notes.txt
<span class="t-loc">src/OrderService.cs:5      </span> <span class="t-sev t-error">failure</span> <span class="t-rule">P001</span>  Placeholder left in change: "YOUR_API_KEY"
<span class="t-loc">src/OrderService.cs:9      </span> <span class="t-sev t-warning">warning</span> <span class="t-rule">P002</span>  Stub left in change: "throw new NotImplementedException("
<span class="t-loc">tests/CalculatorTests.cs:14</span> <span class="t-sev t-error">failure</span> <span class="t-rule">P003</span>  Test "Multiply_Works" has no assertion.</code></pre>
    <figcaption>Check run from a test pull request seeded with one example of each check, under the advisory setting.</figcaption>
</figure>

<section class="section">
    <h2>Configuration</h2>
    <p>Optional. Add <code>.github/aibysitter.json</code> to the repository. The App reads it from the pull request's head commit.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "scope": ["src/**", "tests/**"],
  "conclusion": "fail-on-errors",
  "disable": ["P002"],
  "comment": true
}</code></pre>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Key</th>
                <th>Values</th>
                <th>Default</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>scope</code></td>
                <td>Path globs from the repository root. <code>**</code> matches any number of folders and must be a whole segment (<code>**/*.cs</code>, not <code>**.cs</code>); <code>*</code> and <code>?</code> match within one folder. Case-sensitive. Not supported: <code>{a,b}</code>, <code>[...]</code>, <code>!</code>, <code>\</code>. Turns on P004.</td>
                <td>Not set; P004 is off</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>conclusion</code></td>
                <td><code>advisory</code> reports findings as neutral. <code>fail-on-errors</code> fails the check when any Error finding exists.</td>
                <td><code>advisory</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>disable</code></td>
                <td>Check IDs to skip, for example <code>["P002"]</code>; disabled checks do not run and show as disabled in the check summary. Rule IDs (<code>R001</code>–<code>R016</code>) skip that rule inside P014. <code>aibysitter-disable</code> comments in a rules file apply first.</td>
                <td>None</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>comment</code></td>
                <td><code>true</code> posts one comment on the pull request with the summary table and up to 25 findings linked to their lines. Each new commit updates the same comment. No comment is created while there are no findings.</td>
                <td><code>false</code></td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The config file is itself a changed file: a pull request that edits it outside the declared scope gets a P004 finding. Invalid entries fall back to their defaults, are listed in the check summary and are annotated on their line of the config file. Under <code>fail-on-errors</code>, any config error fails the check.</p>
    <p><a asp-page="/GitHub/Config">Generate a config file</a></p>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <h2>Security model</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Every webhook is verified against its HMAC-SHA256 signature; unsigned or mis-signed deliveries are rejected.</li>
        <li>The App acts as each installation with short-lived installation tokens. The App's private key stays on the server.</li>
        <li>Its only write permission is Checks. It cannot push, comment, merge, or change settings.</li>
        <li>Checks are static text analysis. Code from the pull request is never run.</li>
        <li>It reads at the pull request's head commit only, with fixed caps: file contents for at most @Aibysitter.Web.GitHub.ReviewProcessor.MaxContentFetches changed files, @Aibysitter.Web.GitHub.ReviewProcessor.MaxUnchangedRulesFiles unchanged rules files and @Aibysitter.Web.GitHub.ReviewProcessor.MaxManifestFetches manifests per review.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>What it reads, keeps and logs: <a asp-page="/Privacy">Privacy</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>Install coming soon. Until then, the same rules-file checks are available on the <a asp-page="/Lint">lint page</a>.</p>
    <p>To uninstall: <strong>Settings → Applications → Installed GitHub Apps → Aibysitter → Configure → Uninstall</strong> (organizations: <strong>Settings → GitHub Apps</strong>). Details: <a asp-page="/Privacy">Privacy</a>.</p>
</section>
